  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P3] Short-circuit empty input before querying",
      "body": "Previously `loadUsers([])` resolved to `[]` via `Promise.all([])` without touching the database. The new code unconditionally awaits `findMany({ where: { id: { in: [] } } })`, adding a wasted round trip for an inherently empty result, and on adapters that reject empty `IN` lists (or when the database is unavailable) a call that always succeeded can now reject. A trivial guard restores the old behavior: `if (ids.length === 0) return [];`",
      "severity": "P3",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/users.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 22,
        "end": 23
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P3] Confirm `null` is the intended not-found sentinel",
      "body": "The old implementation returned each `db.users.find(id)` result verbatim; `byId.get(id) ?? null` now normalizes missing rows to `null`. If this adapter's `find` resolves `undefined` for unknown ids, callers distinguishing `undefined` from `null` (e.g. strict `=== undefined` checks) see a changed return contract, despite the PR description stating existing contracts are preserved. `db` is not declared anywhere in this repo (pre-existing), so the previous sentinel cannot be confirmed from source — worth verifying against the actual adapter, or mapping to whatever `find` used to return.",
      "severity": "P3",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/users.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 25,
        "end": 25
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P3] Confirm the adapter handles large `in` lists",
      "body": "The change goes from N single-parameter queries to one statement with one bind parameter per unique id, and `ids` is unbounded. Many adapters cap parameters per statement (SQLite ~999 by default, SQL Server 2100); above the cap the single `findMany` fails outright where the per-id version did not. If large input lists are realistic, chunk `uniqueIds` into batches and merge the resulting maps.",
      "severity": "P3",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/users.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 23,
        "end": 23
      }
    }
  ],
